The main-B workflow is saved (version 4), but I couldn't check that it starts a call: the one-turn chat test came back with 402 "Insufficient credits", so no live test ran.

`out/main-B.workflow.json` already existed from an earlier main-B build this morning, with the same layout: date-facts start node, opening, identity, account lookup, negotiation, end_call. I updated that file rather than starting over:
- **Date code:** I replaced the start node with the `code_node` from `main-B.calc.json`, unedited and pointing to the opening node. I set the `get_account` `post_process_code` to `account_post_process_code` exactly as given.
- **Add-note rule:** the agent now calls `add_note` for every product without a promise, also with a single product and when no promise is made. It adds no notes at all when the call is transferred. Earlier it only did this with two or more products. I followed Brief B rule 8 here; Brief A alone never uses `add_note`. This is a judgement call worth checking.
- **Failed `create_promise`:** after two failures the agent keeps the promises already recorded, adds a `service_error` note for that product, and closes as `no_promise` / `service_error` if nothing was recorded.

Lint shows no errors or warnings. The wording gate shows no errors and one warning, the number "250.00" in the `create_promise` amount description, which is only an example value. The brief's date rules match the date facts, so nothing differs there.

